 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” lawyer for every Houston car-wreck case. A reasonable starting point is **Terry Bryant**: his profile lists Texas Board of Legal Specialization certification in Personal Injury Trial Law and repeated Super Lawyers selections. **Paul H. Cannon** is another option; his firm says he is board-certified in personal injury trial law and has handled car-accident cases.\n\nTreat awards and firm claims as leads, not guarantees. Before hiring, ask who will personally handle your case, how often they take cases to trial, what similar cases they’ve handled, and how fees and case expenses work. Verify the lawyer’s license and certification, and compare a couple of consultations. The **Houston Lawyer Referral Service** offers screened referrals at **713-237-9429**; the State Bar of Texas also lists certified referral services.\n\nIf you share whether the wreck involved serious injuries, a commercial vehicle, or a disputed fault, I can suggest what experience to prioritize.",
